Hello, this is Sumanth. Today marks Day 9 of my Cloud Architect journey.
Date : 20-05-2026
Day : Wednesday

GOAL:
Build cloud fundamentals, understand AWS core concepts, and achieve the first milestone in the Cloud Architect journey through certification-based learning.

====================================================
AWS CLOUD FUNDAMENTALS
====================================================

1. What is Cloud Computing

Definition:
Cloud computing is the delivery of computing services such as servers, storage, databases, networking, software, and analytics over the internet.

Purpose:
Access resources on demand without managing physical infrastructure.


2. Cloud Computing Benefits

Benefits:
Scalability
Elasticity
High Availability
Cost Optimization
Global Reach
Pay-as-you-go pricing
Faster deployment

Purpose:
Understand why organizations adopt cloud solutions.


3. Cloud Service Models

IaaS:
Infrastructure as a Service

Examples:
AWS EC2
Virtual Machines
Storage

Purpose:
Manage infrastructure resources.


PaaS:
Platform as a Service

Examples:
Application hosting platforms

Purpose:
Focus on application deployment without infrastructure management.


SaaS:
Software as a Service

Examples:
Gmail
Office 365
Salesforce

Purpose:
Consume ready-made software over the internet.


====================================================
AWS CORE CONCEPTS
====================================================

4. AWS Global Infrastructure

Concepts:
Regions
Availability Zones
Edge Locations

Purpose:
Understand AWS physical/global architecture.


Definitions:

Region:
Geographical area containing AWS data centers

Availability Zone:
Isolated data center location inside a region

Edge Location:
Content delivery locations closer to users


5. Shared Responsibility Model

AWS Responsibilities:
Physical security
Infrastructure
Networking hardware
Managed services backend

Customer Responsibilities:
Applications
Operating systems
Passwords
Data
Configurations
Access management

Purpose:
Understand security ownership in cloud.


